  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### CAPIUM 365: Adding Bank Statements Via CSV or PDF\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 9 Oct, 2025 at 10:20 AM\n\n\t\tAdding Bank Statements Via CSV or PDF\n\nYou can upload statements in bulk if you prefer not to use a bank feed.\n\nNavigation:Capium 365 > Client > Settings (top right) > Imports > Bank Statements\n\nSteps:\n\nClick the Settings (cog icon) in the top right of Capium.\n\nSelect \"Imports\".\n\nChoose \"Bank Statements\" and click Next.\n\nSelect the format you want to upload (PDF or Excel/CSV).\n\nUpload the statement file into Capium.\n\nNote: If you upload via CSV you can download a template file and upload it back into Capium.\n\nSee screenshot below for reference:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
